  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilient Livelihoods, Positive Coping: Overcoming barriers to Yemeni children&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s wellbeing created by the socioeconomic impact of Covid-19.The project will deliver improved socio-economic conditions and education access for vulnerable families in BaniHushaish, Sana&apos;a, who are facing deepening poverty due to the economic impact of Covid-19. A sustainable package oflivelihood, child protection and education support will ensure households can meet their basic needs within 18 monthsand avoid negative coping mechanisms that place their children, and girls in particular, out of school and at risk of earlymarriage and child labour.</narrative>
  </description>
